    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Parks",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S6945\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\nAn act to authorize the village of Plandome Heights to discontinue the\nuse of certain land as parkland\n\n\n PURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL :\nTo allow for the Village of Plandome Heights to convey a portion of\nthe land known as Section 3, Block 28, Lot 295, which is used by the\nVillage as parkland, in order to resolve an adverse possession claim\non a portion of the parkland.\n\n SUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS :\nSection one of the bill authorizes the Village of Plandome Heights\nBoard of Trustees to discontinue and convey the disputed plot of\nparkland in exchange for fair market value.\n\nSection three requires that the fair market value received in exchange\nfor the certain plot of land must be used by the village of Plandome\nHeights for the acquisition of new parklands of at least equal fair\nmarket value or for capital improvements to existing park facilities.\n\nSection four describes the location and boundaries of the parkland to\nbe conveyed.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\nIn 2006 a claim of adverse possession was made over a portion of Lot\n295, to which the Village of Plandome Heights held title.  It is\nunclear, as a matter of law, whether Lot 295 was used by the Village\nas parkland or for proprietary purposes before the litigation was\ninitiated, however since the claim was made the village has begun to\nuse the undisputed area of Lot 295 as parkland. At this time, the\nundisputed portion of Lot 295 is used by the Village as parkland.\n\nIn 2007, the adverse possession claim survived a motion to dismiss\nmade by the Village on the ground that it was a question of fact as to\nwhether Lot 295 was used as parkland or for proprietary purposes, and\nthe claimants were granted a preliminary injunction to continue using\nthe disputed area. Instead of burdening taxpayers with costly\nlitigation, the Village has reached a settlement agreement with the\nclaimants that would convey to them the disputed portion of Lot 295 in\nreturn for fair market value.\n\nIt will no longer be decided whether, as a matter of law, Lot 295 is\nor is not parkland. However, since the village now considers Lot 295\nas parkland, it must receive authority from the New York State\nLegislature to convey the disputed property to the claimants, and the\nsettlement is conditioned upon this authorization.\n\n PRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\nThis is a new bill.\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\nNone to the state.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
